# Trivy findings accepted on purpose. Each has a reason and an expiry (exp:), after which CI fails
# again and the decision must be revisited. Tracked in docs/security/threat-model.md (accepted risks).

# Redshift security group allows egress to 0.0.0.0/0 (infra/terraform/main.tf, aws_security_group.redshift).
# Redshift Serverless likely needs no SG egress (enhanced VPC routing is off), so the rule can probably be
# removed -- but that's a live AWS change: it needs the owner's approval and a planned apply to verify COPY
# from S3 still works. Accepted until then.
AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2027-01-31

# The S3 bucket is encrypted with SSE-S3 (AES256), not a customer-managed KMS key. It holds synthetic data
# only; a CMK costs ~$1/month plus requests against limited credits and adds no protection for dummy data.
# Revisit before any real data lands in the bucket.
AVD-AWS-0132 exp:2027-01-31
